2186544806 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544806 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-3,1]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544806 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c4eccd2-7dd0-53ca-8b67-e044fcc594a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544806 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}\\le \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})-\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})\\le {y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})-\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le \\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}-\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{j-1}+{x}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{2}-(-3)^{2})(4-2)=-8 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})(1-(-3))=24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 24-(-8)\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 32\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=32.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544824 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544824 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123747" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544824 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544824 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [3,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=4y-2x+3.$ Further, let \n\n$$\nI={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\,\\le I\\,\\le U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums, and \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\n$$\n\nWhat expression is missing from the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544824 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "60f150de-1cdb-534e-a48d-461dca7bdb52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544824 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $L(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=4y-2x+3$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=4y-2x+3$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=4{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+3\n$$\n\nand the lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544863 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544863 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123850" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544863 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544863 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(8-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(8-2{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following results:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0}) \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}-{x}_{0})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544863 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ac9755ca-22ae-5d63-a731-5137b2daeebf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544863 #edb/ref 1074 "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n8-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}\\le 8-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 8-2{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n8-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}\\le 8-({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 8-2{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[8-({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le 8{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,-\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})(3-2)=4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2}-{2}^{2})(2-0)=5 \\\\ 8{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =8(2-0)(3-2)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 16-4-5\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 7\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=7.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
